WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.126
Quick question. Who made your phone case?

2
00:00:03.256 --> 00:00:06.685
And how many companies touched it
before it landed in your hands?

3
00:00:06.815 --> 00:00:10.307
Hint: it's more than one.
Welcome to the marketing channel.

4
00:00:11.657 --> 00:00:16.376
A marketing channel is all the
individuals and firms involved in making a

5
00:00:16.376 --> 00:00:20.633
product or service available to
consumers or industrial users.

6
00:00:20.763 --> 00:00:23.035
Think of it as the
route a product travels,

7
00:00:23.035 --> 00:00:24.447
from the maker to you.

8
00:00:25.797 --> 00:00:28.650
Picture four kayak makers
and four shoppers.

9
00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:31.502
If every maker sells to
every shopper directly,

10
00:00:31.502 --> 00:00:33.489
that's sixteen separate deals.

11
00:00:33.619 --> 00:00:37.133
Now put one intermediary, like
a retailer, in the middle.

12
00:00:37.263 --> 00:00:40.286
Four plus four. Eight
contacts. Half the work.

13
00:00:40.416 --> 00:00:43.201
That's reason number one
intermediaries exist.

14
00:00:43.201 --> 00:00:45.509
They make exchange more efficient.

15
00:00:46.859 --> 00:00:50.437
Intermediaries also do real
work, in three functions.

16
00:00:50.567 --> 00:00:53.733
Transactional: buying,
selling, and taking on risk,

17
00:00:53.733 --> 00:00:57.025
like owning inventory that
might go out of style.

18
00:00:57.155 --> 00:00:59.617
Logistical: assorting, storing, sorting,

19
00:00:59.617 --> 00:01:02.759
and transporting. Basically,
the heavy lifting.

20
00:01:02.889 --> 00:01:05.709
And facilitating:
financing, grading quality,

21
00:01:05.709 --> 00:01:08.089
and sharing marketing information.

22
00:01:09.439 --> 00:01:13.123
All that work creates value
for buyers, in four utilities.

23
00:01:13.253 --> 00:01:15.829
Time utility: it's there when you want it.

24
00:01:15.959 --> 00:01:18.321
Place utility: it's where you want it.

25
00:01:18.451 --> 00:01:21.645
Form utility: it's improved
to be more appealing.

26
00:01:21.775 --> 00:01:24.957
And possession utility: you
can actually take it home,

27
00:01:24.957 --> 00:01:26.739
even if you pay over time.

28
00:01:28.089 --> 00:01:31.045
So the next time someone
says, cut out the middleman,

29
00:01:31.045 --> 00:01:32.245
ask one question.

30
00:01:32.373 --> 00:01:34.309
Who's going to do all that work?

